From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Keep SSE2 enabled by default only on x86 targets
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Upstream-Version: 1.15
Upstream-Status: Not submitted; package-local architecture default fix
Source: Fixed official libsquish 1.15 CMakeLists.txt
Remove-When: An official release selects compatible architecture defaults

SSE2 instructions and -msse2 are x86-specific. Keep the existing x86
default, while selecting the already supplied scalar backend by default
on other targets. Explicit option overrides and other features remain
unchanged. This adds no new codec implementation.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -18,1 +18,7 @@
-OPTION(BUILD_SQUISH_WITH_SSE2 "Build with SSE2." ON)
+SET(SQUISH_SSE2_DEFAULT OFF)
+STRING(TOLOWER "${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR}" SQUISH_TARGET_PROCESSOR)
+IF (SQUISH_TARGET_PROCESSOR MATCHES "^(i[3-6]86|x86|x86_64|amd64|x64)$")
+    SET(SQUISH_SSE2_DEFAULT ON)
+ENDIF ()
+OPTION(BUILD_SQUISH_WITH_SSE2 "Build with SSE2." ${SQUISH_SSE2_DEFAULT})
+UNSET(SQUISH_SSE2_DEFAULT)
